# End-of-turn work report + status board (chat)

When this Cursor chat is the **Sume main agent**, Chase reads **this
chat**. Slack `#coding-agents` is a team mirror. It does **not** replace
the report in this thread.

## Work report (body of the turn)

Write a report Chase can follow **without opening Slack, the canvas, or
a worker log**. Same language as Chase. Do this even when you also
posted a Slack parent or reply that turn.

Required when anything material happened (plan, fire, worker signal,
PR/MQ, dest/prod, a lock, a blocker):

- What you did / found (nouns, URLs, SHAs, issue/PR numbers in the
  prose — not “see Slack”)
- Decisions and open waits (who owes the next lock)
- Evidence in-line (counts, endpoints, file paths). Secrets stay out.

**Chase lock (2026-08-26):** do **not** write 완료 / done / completed /
landed / “들어갔습니다” until `git fetch origin main && git log
origin/main --oneline --grep='(#N)'` shows the commit. Enqueue, green
PR checks, Ready, and Graphite “Your changes” are **not** 완료. Say
what is true (queued / ejected / still OPEN).

Forbidden as the whole turn:

- Board tables only
- “Slack에 올렸다” / thread link with no body
- Pointing Chase at `#coding-agents` to understand the work

A short “nothing moved” turn still needs one sentence of state, then
the board. Do not skip the board because the turn was a rule edit.

## Status board (last block)

Every turn **ends** by reprinting the **status board** as markdown
tables. The board is an **index**, not the report.

Board definition (lanes, confirm = resolve, 24h → 백로그, Job titles):

`~/.cursor/rules/status-board.mdc`

Last user-visible block. One-shot reconcile — no poll loops.

Always print **`지금`** + **`스테이징`**. Print **`백로그`** when it
has rows. Identifiers stay English.

Canvas is the same board (`active-workers-canvas.mdc`) — chat report +
board are mandatory even when the canvas and Slack are current.
